      "content": "It is true that some data, particularly in specific policy contexts, suggests that certain benefit levels can create stronger disincentives for full-time, higher-earning work. This is often attributed to the \"poverty trap,\" where the benefit loss through earning a little more outweighs the gain in income. However, it is crucial to differentiate between *discouraging full-time, high-wage work* versus *preventing essential survival work*, as the overall impact is heavily debated in the literature.",
